# --- LLVM toolchain (build-time only) for edk2 -------------------------------
# QEMU's prebuilt edk2-aarch64-code.fd is built without SECURE_BOOT_ENABLE, so
# it cannot enforce Secure Boot (verified: no SecureBoot/SetupMode variables).
# build.sh rebuilds ArmVirtQemu from the edk2 sources inside the QEMU tarball
# (roms/edk2, edk2-stable202408, all submodules included) with Secure Boot on,
# using edk2's CLANGDWARF toolchain, which needs clang + lld + llvm-ar +
# llvm-objcopy for an ELF aarch64 target (Apple's toolchain has no ELF linker).
# Official LLVM release binary for macOS arm64. Hash source: GitHub release
# asset digest (api.github.com, release llvmorg-22.1.8). Only bin/ and lib/clang
# are extracted into build/tools/llvm. Not copied into build/qemu-src (1.5 GB;
# a compiler, not part of the corresponding source); fetched from this URL.
LLVM_VERSION=22.1.8
LLVM_FILE=LLVM-22.1.8-macOS-ARM64.tar.xz
LLVM_URL=https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/releases/download/llvmorg-22.1.8/LLVM-22.1.8-macOS-ARM64.tar.xz
LLVM_SHA256=f260f4f7c0d430828a81ae8a3826a1d63fc0963ec2459489308cc23b1f7eab4f

